  "coverImage": "https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/lmstudio-datasette-agent.webp",
  "readTime": 1,
  "content": "<p><strong>Release:</strong> <a href=\"https://github.com/datasette/datasette-llm/releases/tag/0.1a11\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-llm 0.1a11</a></p>\n<p><code>datasette-llm</code> is the intermediate plugin for Datasette that supports configuring LLMs for use with other Datasette plugins.</p>\n<p>This release adds support for OpenAI-compatible endpoints, so you can configure Datasette to use an LLM hosted anywhere that talks the OpenAI pseudo-standard web protocol.</p>\n<p>This means that if you're running local models with <a href=\"https://lmstudio.ai\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">LM Studio</a> or <a href=\"https://ollama.com\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Ollama</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">llama.cpp</a> (which just hit <a href=\"https://huggingface.co/blog/ggml-org/llama-cpp-v1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">v1.0.0</a>) you can run Datasette via <code>uvx</code> like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-shell\"><pre>wget https://datasette.io/content.db\n\nuvx --with datasette-agent datasette \\\n  --root --secret 1 \\\n  -s plugins.datasette-llm.default_model <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span>{</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">    \"model\": \"lmstudio-qwen\",</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">    \"model_name\": \"qwen/qwen3.8-27b\",</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">    \"api_base\": \"http://localhost:1234/v1\"</span>\n<span class=\"pl-s\">  }<span class=\"pl-pds\">'</span></span> content.db</pre></div>\n<p>And you'll get a local server running a Datasette Agent instance powered by your local model!</p>\n<p><img alt='Screenshot of a chat interface. Header bar reads \"home\" on the left and \"root\" with a hamburger menu icon on the right. Below is a back arrow, the heading \"Chat\", a model label \"lmstudio-qwen\" and an \"EXPORT\" button. A blue user message bubble says \"how many repos and how many releases are there?\" Below it is a collapsed tool call \"list_databases_and_tables\" and an expanded tool call \"sql_query\". Its REQUEST section shows database \"content\", display \"both\" and the SQL: SELECT (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM repos) AS repo_count, (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM releases) AS release_count. Its RESPONSE section shows columns repo_count and release_count with a single row of 200 and 1889. Below that is a table with columns repo_count and release_count and one row: 200, 1889, followed by a \"View SQL query\" button. The assistant reply reads \"There are 200 repos and 1,889 releases in the content database.\" At the bottom is a text input with placeholder \"Type a message... (# to tag a table or query)\" and a blue \"Send\" button.' loading=\"lazy\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" src=\"https://static.simonwillison.net/static/2026/lmstudio-datasette-agent.webp\"/></p>\n<p>Tags: <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/uv\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">uv</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette-agent\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette-agent</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">llm</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/datasette\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">datasette</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/llms\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">llms</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/ai\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">ai</a>, <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/tags/generative-ai\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">generative-ai</a></p>",
